            "review_text": "Cruiser02023515684\n6 contributions\n0\nGreat place for time with friends\nFeb 2024 • Friends\nI've known about La Haye since a friend invited me to a birthday party last March. Now that I have the opportunity to stop by, I'm really surprised by the quality of the food and the service style here. Back then, the dish was ok, but today I find it even more delicious. We went in a large group so we were able to try many dishes. We ordered French fries, scallop noodles, Shrimp salad,... I love the potato patat here because the accompanying sauce is quite delicious (especially the garlic mayo sauce). . Scallop noodles are always very special, mixing the noodles with the accompanying sauce and eating with fresh scallops is an experience you must try when you come here. The staff serve enthusiastically and also advise very carefully about the dishes, which is a plus point that I highly appreciate for La Haye.\n\nThe restaurant is located at the foot of Ba Son bridge, very close to the city center, so if you have the opportunity, come experience it.\nRead more\nShow original\nWritten March 13, 2024",
